1
00:00:05,298 --> 00:00:09,548
(Leonard:)Hey, can I talk to you about something?
It's a little awkward.

2
00:00:09,719 --> 00:00:12,099
(Sheldon:)I know what this is about.

3
00:00:12,263 --> 00:00:14,433
(Sheldon:)Given the professional standstill
you're at...

4
00:00:14,599 --> 00:00:17,189
(Sheldon:)...you're wondering
if this is the appropriate time...

5
00:00:17,352 --> 00:00:20,232
(Sheldon:)...to abandon your research
and focus on teaching.

6
00:00:24,651 --> 00:00:25,901
(Howard:)Yes.

7
00:00:27,528 --> 00:00:30,368
(Sheldon:)And if I may suggest,
consider changing disciplines.

8
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:33,451
(Sheldon:)Yeah, to the humanities.
Perhaps, history.

9
00:00:33,618 --> 00:00:35,698
(Sheldon:)One of the advantages
of teaching history...

10
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:38,040
(Sheldon:)...is that you don't have
to create things.

11
00:00:38,206 --> 00:00:40,996
(Sheldon:)You know, you just have to remember
stuff that happened...

12
00:00:41,167 --> 00:00:43,377
(Sheldon:)...and then parrot it back.

13
00:00:43,670 --> 00:00:45,380
(Sheldon:)You could have fun with that.

14
00:00:46,673 --> 00:00:48,213
(Leonard:)Yeah, that's not it.

15
00:00:48,383 --> 00:00:50,673
(Leonard:)Stuart's kind of interested in Amy.

16
00:00:50,843 --> 00:00:53,093
Well, of course, he is.
She's very interesting.

17
00:00:53,263 --> 00:00:55,223
(Sheldon:)Did you know, when she was 14...

18
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:57,930
(Sheldon:)...she severed the webbing
between her own toes?

19
00:01:00,061 --> 00:01:02,061
No. Uh...

